              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Urdu for a point (that things come to), then the Urdu for supposing (for argument's sake)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: بہرحال",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بہرحال — baharhāl — \"anyway; in any case\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بہرحال، اگر آپ آئے تو ہمیں خوشی ہو گی۔ baharhāl, agar āp āe to hameṅ khushī ho gī. Anyway, if you come, we will be glad."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "بہرحال (baharhāl) is usually traced to Persian ba-har-ḥāl, \"in every state\", built from ba, \"in\", har, \"every\", and Arabic ḥāl, \"a state\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for saying what happens if."
